<$transclude $tiddler="$:/plugins/rimir/doc-template/templates/page">
<$fill $name="body">

!! Which tiddlers can be outlined?

Wikitext tiddlers (`text/vnd.tiddlywiki`) that are not drafts, system tiddlers, `code-body` or `hide-body` tiddlers. v1 is wikitext only; Markdown comes later through a second format adapter.

!! How do I switch it on?

You don't: Ctrl-Click (Cmd-Click on Mac) on a block wakes the outline of that tiddler. Escape with nothing selected, a click outside the tiddler or closing it puts it back to sleep. Leave a single tiddler out with the field `outline: no`, or all of them with the //Enabled// setting.

!! Does it slow down a story with many tiddlers?

No. An idle tiddler has one extra widget and a few event listeners; it parses nothing, stamps nothing and does no work when its text changes. Waking needs no re-render.

!! A plugin shows a tiddler with its own body template: no outline?

Right. The outline's body filter only takes a tiddler whose body would otherwise be the core default, so any other body template wins and that tiddler gets no outline.

!! How do I put a heading above a list or paragraph?

Select the list (or paragraph, or lower heading), Alt-Enter, and pick a heading under //Insert before//. Or insert it anywhere after and press Alt-Up: a heading moves up over the blocks above it.

!! Can I move a unit into another list or section?

Across heading lines, yes: a paragraph or list at the end of a section moves down into the next section, the first block of a section moves up out of it, and a heading moves up over the blocks above it (they join its section). List items stay in their list and blocks stay in their HTML container. To take a unit anywhere else, into another list, section or tiddler: Ctrl-X, select the place, Ctrl-V; the paste adapts its levels.

!! Can I paste a copied unit into an e-mail?

Yes. Ctrl-C on a selected unit puts it on the system clipboard as HTML (rendered: lists, headings, tables, code; TiddlyWiki's styles do not come along, links to tiddlers become plain text) and as its wikitext. E-mail, Jira and other rich text editors paste the HTML, plain text fields the wikitext. Pasted back into an outline, also in another wiki, the levels adapt to the place.

!! Are widgets and macros editable inside?

No. `<$list>`, `<$reveal>`, macro and procedure calls are single units: select, move or edit their source as a whole. Only plain HTML containers are opened.

!! Plugins that replace core widgets (copy buttons on code blocks, ...)?

A plugin can replace a core widget with its own `\widget` definition, for example `$codeblock` (kookma's utility plugin adds a caption and a copy button). The replacement renders without source positions; outline assigns it to the next unit of that type in document order, and frames, edits and moves it like any other block. What it renders inside stays untouched.

!! Why can't I select a block?

Units that render nothing (for example a procedure call with empty output) have no DOM node and cannot be selected.

!! What happens when I save an empty unit?

A unit without children is deleted. A unit with children is not: the save is refused with a notice. A new unit (from Enter) that stays empty writes nothing.

!! What if the tiddler changes while I edit?

Your text is kept. On save the unit is looked up again by its original source: if it occurs exactly once, the save goes there; otherwise the editor stays open with a notice.

!! Two views of the same tiddler?

Only one view can edit at a time.

!! What happens to an unsaved edit?

Escape or toggling outline mode off discards it. If you changed the text and the view is rendered again (for example after a global macro changed) or you close the tiddler, the text is kept: the editor opens again at the unit as soon as the tiddler is shown in outline mode. If the unit is gone by then, the editor opens with the "changed underneath" notice, so you can copy your text. Kept text lives in a `$:/temp/` tiddler and is gone after a reload.

!! Why does Alt-Up/Down add a blank line?

When a list, code block or table is followed directly (single line break) by a paragraph, swapping them as they are would merge the paragraph with its new neighbour. Such blocks get a blank line between them. Items and headings keep their line breaks.

A comment (or other text that is not a unit) between the two blocks is kept and set apart by blank lines too.

!! Why does Alt-Up/Down sometimes do nothing?

A move swaps a unit with its neighbour inside the same parent (an item only with an item of the same level, a heading with a heading of the same level) or moves it across one heading line (see the reference); at the first or last place there is nothing to move over. Before writing, outline re-parses the result; if the swap would change the units (for example a heading section whose last paragraph would merge with the next block), the move is refused and the text stays unchanged. Add a blank line between the blocks by hand and try again.

!! Do Tab and Alt-Up/Down work while I edit?

Yes. They save your text, indent, promote or move the unit with its subtree, and keep editing it at its new place with the cursor where it was. With empty text they do nothing.

!! My CSS for `.tc-tiddler-body > p` stopped working

The body of every eligible tiddler is wrapped in `div.rr-ol` (idle or awake), so child selectors of `.tc-tiddler-body` no longer match. Use a descendant selector (`.tc-tiddler-body p`) or also match `.tc-tiddler-body > .rr-ol > p`.

!! Do `AI:` lines of llm-inline fire?

No. Outline writes bypass `th-saving-tiddler`, which llm-inline listens to. `AI:` lines typed in outline mode do not fire; they do after a normal editor save.

!! Why doesn't the editor show the `*` or `!`?

The editor edits a unit's content. The list marker and the heading level are structure: change them with Tab/Shift-Tab. If you type the item's own marker at the start anyway (for example `* ` in a `*` item), it is dropped instead of doubled.

!! How do I put a line break into a bullet?

Shift-Enter in the editor. In wikitext a list item (and a heading) is one source line, and a real line break would end it: the next line would become a paragraph that swallows the following items. So line breaks in items and headings are saved as `<br>`, and an existing `<br>` shows as a line break when you edit. Enter stays //save and new item//. Paragraphs and other blocks keep real line breaks.

!! Why can't a paragraph of several lines become a heading or a bullet?

A heading and a list item are one source line. Several lines would have to be squeezed into one with `<br>`, which changes the text more than a type switch should. Join the lines first, or turn it into a quote block or code block.

!! How do I add Graphviz or Mermaid diagrams?

Install rimir/graphviz or rimir/mermaid. Each registers a block type: //Insert after → Graphviz graph// writes a `$$$text/vnd.graphviz` block, and on a bullet //Add to this item → Graphviz graph// creates a graph tiddler and transcludes it in the item. A double-click on the graph (or Shift-Enter on its line) opens its source with a live preview in an overlay; Ctrl-Enter saves.

!! Can I edit a transcluded tiddler where it is shown?

Select its line (or the bullet) and press Shift-Enter: it opens in an overlay right there, with its own outline. Escape (twice: first the selection) closes it. Ctrl-Shift-Enter opens it in the story instead.

!! How do I move several blocks at once?

Select the first, then Shift-Down (or Shift-Click the last): the range is framed, Alt-Up/Down, Tab, Delete, Ctrl-C/X and Externalize take all of it.

!! Why is Externalize missing for some sub-items?

Sub-items move into a list that is transcluded at the end of their parent's line, so it renders before the parent's other sub-items. A range that does not start at the parent's first sub-item would change the order; select from the first one (or move them up first).

!! How does another plugin add a block type?

With one tiddler tagged `$:/tags/rimir/outline/BlockType` (see the reference: block types). For a content type with its own parser, `behaviour: typed` and `content-type` are enough; `contexts: block item` and `inline: transclude` add it to bullets as a transcluded tiddler.

!! Why does switching one bullet to numbered switch its neighbours too?

In wikitext the list type is the marker character, and items of one level with different characters do not form one list: one numbered item among bullets would cut the list into three. So //Turn into// switches all items of that level under the same parent; their sub-items keep their own type.

!! Do editor plugins work?

Yes, the editor is TW's own edit widget. AutoComplete handles Enter, Escape, Tab and the arrows first; outline keys act only if the event was not consumed.

!! Does Tab leave the page?

No, while a unit is selected Tab is used for indent.

